pbwatch for Debian
------------------

After installing this package, complete the setup manually:

1. Find your Pixel Buds Bluetooth address:

     bluetoothctl devices

2. Create ~/.config/pbwatch/config.toml with your MAC address:

     mkdir -p ~/.config/pbwatch
     echo 'macs = ["AB:CD:EF:01:23:45"]' >> ~/.config/pbwatch/config.toml

   A fully commented example config is available at:
     /usr/share/doc/pbwatch/examples/config.toml

3. Enable and start the background service:

     systemctl --user enable --now pbwatch

To check the service status:

     systemctl --user status pbwatch
     journalctl --user -u pbwatch -n 30

To apply config changes, restart the service:

     systemctl --user restart pbwatch


Multiple pairs
--------------

Add all MAC addresses to the macs list in config.toml:

     macs = ["AB:CD:EF:01:23:45", "12:34:56:78:9A:BC"]

pbwatch will monitor all pairs and send a separate notification for each.


Notification daemon
-------------------

pbwatch sends standard desktop notifications (freedesktop.org spec).
It works with any notification daemon: dunst, mako, SwayNC, GNOME, KDE.

For dunst, add the following rule to ~/.config/dunst/dunstrc to display
the battery widget at full size:

     [pbwatch]
         appname = pbwatch
         format = "%b"
         icon_position = left
         min_icon_size = 0
         max_icon_size = 320

See /usr/share/doc/pbwatch/ for additional documentation.

